{#- Why a planner reply, or a planning call, was not accepted: one rendering per typed problem. -#}
{% from '_reply_errors.j2' import error_path, reply_errors %}
{% macro alternatives(items) -%}
{% if items %}{% for item in items %}({{ quoted(item.hypothesis_id) }}, {{ quoted(item.revision) }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}none{% endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
{% macro quoted(text) -%}
'{{ text }}'
{%- endmacro %}
{% macro violation(item) -%}
{{ error_path(item.path) }}: {% if item.code.value == 'over-capacity' -%}
portfolio requested {{ item.requested }} workstreams, but capacity is {{ item.capacity }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'duplicate-id' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} repeats an earlier entry's ID; merge the entries or give each its own ID
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-id-used' -%}
hypothesis ID {{ quoted(item.subject) }} was already used
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-abandoned' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is abandoned and cannot be continued
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-in-flight' -%}
hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }} is still in flight
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-unknown' -%}
unknown hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }} cannot be continued
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-terminal' -%}
evaluated hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }} is already terminal
{%- elif item.code.value == 'hypothesis-blocked' -%}
hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }} was blocked; continue it only with a task that removes the recorded blocker, or park or abandon it
{%- elif item.code.value == 'revision-without-parent' -%}
an exact candidate revision requires {{ reply.parent_hypothesis_id }}; usable options: {{ alternatives(item.usable) }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'continuation-has-parent' -%}
a continued hypothesis builds on its own candidate; use null
{%- elif item.code.value == 'revision-not-offered' -%}
{{ quoted(item.revision) }} is not an offered revision of {{ quoted(item.subject) }}; usable options: {{ alternatives(item.usable) }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'parent-not-buildable' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is not a buildable candidate; name one listed under buildable candidates (for a merge, its latest verified candidate), or use null for the main revision
{%- elif item.code.value == 'profile-not-offered' -%}
this run cannot produce trusted profile evidence; schedule only implement workstreams
{%- elif item.code.value == 'profile-fields-unsupported' -%}
this run's capture cannot supply {{ item.fields | join(', ') }}; require only fields it supplies (supplied: {{ item.supplied | join(', ') or 'none' }})
{%- elif item.code.value == 'profile-id-used' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} was already used; choose a new ID
{%- elif item.code.value == 'update-running' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is still running; park or abandon it only after its workstream finishes
{%- elif item.code.value == 'update-duplicate' -%}
duplicate strategy update for hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'update-unknown' -%}
strategy update names unknown hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'update-incomplete' -%}
cannot update incomplete hypothesis {{ quoted(item.subject) }}
{%- elif item.code.value == 'outside-plan' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is not a failed step of the task's plan; until every step is done, continue only failed steps
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-id-used' -%}
merge ID {{ quoted(item.subject) }} was already used; choose a new ID
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-in-flight' -%}
another merge is running or scheduled; schedule one merge at a time, after the running one finishes
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-candidate-repeated' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is listed twice in this merge; list each candidate once
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-candidate-is-main' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is a merged main, already part of main; merge only candidates listed as mergeable
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-candidate-merged' -%}
the latest candidate of {{ quoted(item.subject) }} is already merged into main; merge only candidates listed as mergeable
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-candidate-not-better' -%}
the latest candidate of {{ quoted(item.subject) }} does not beat main's latest measurement; merge only candidates listed as mergeable
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-baseline-pending' -%}
the input's measurement has not landed, so main has no measurement the latest candidate of {{ quoted(item.subject) }} could be shown to beat; schedule no merge until it lands
{%- elif item.code.value == 'merge-uncheckable' -%}
this task has no trusted accuracy check, so a merged commit could never become main; schedule no merge
{%- elif item.code.value == 'combine-parent-repeated' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is named twice in this combine; name each part's hypothesis once, at one exact offered revision
{%- elif item.code.value == 'expectation-unknown' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is not a workstream of this reply; name only workstreams this reply schedules
{%- elif item.code.value == 'ranking-unknown' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is not a hypothesis or profile of this run; rank only IDs from the history or this reply
{%- elif item.code.value == 'ranking-duplicate' -%}
{{ quoted(item.subject) }} is ranked twice; list each ID once
{%- else -%}
{{ item.code.value }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endmacro %}
